Normalise malformed ELF section alignment for SGI inputs

Upstream commit 9e6619e285873fe1cb002da4bb7749be40a5627c (Alan Modra,
2011-04-20) changed bfd_log2 from rounding down to rounding up. Thus
2.20.1 mapped sh_addralign 27 to alignment power 4 (16), while 2.23.2's
round-up behaviour maps it to power 5 (32). Upstream commit
1f9b1a84350d3755ce8620900a35c3d1997535e6 (Alan Modra, 2022-02-15) then
changed _bfd_elf_make_section_from_shdr from bfd_log2 (sh_addralign) to
bfd_log2 (sh_addralign & -sh_addralign), using the greatest power-of-two
divisor for invalid ELF alignment values. For SGI IRIX crt1.o's .init
sh_addralign of 27, the 2.47 code therefore sets alignment power 0 (1-byte
alignment). The 2.20.1 behaviour placed output .init at 0x400560 and
__istart at 0x40056c; 2.47's alignment 1 placed __istart at 0x40051e in
the failing cand-h image, producing the core's EPC = BADVADDR address
error through GOT slot 18.

The ELF backend section_from_shdr callback is not used for ordinary
SHT_PROGBITS sections. Instead, both MIPS object_p callbacks run after
all section headers have been made into BFD sections. Under SGI_COMPAT
only, restore the pre-change floor normalisation for malformed
non-power-of-two sh_addralign values. Valid ELF alignments and generic
MIPS/Linux inputs are unchanged. This covers both o32 and n32 callbacks;
the actual malformed value occurs in the captured o32 crt1.o.

Provenance: upstream binutils commits 9e6619e285873fe1cb002da4bb7749be40a5627c
and 1f9b1a84350d3755ce8620900a35c3d1997535e6.


--- a/bfd/elf32-mips.c
+++ b/bfd/elf32-mips.c
@@ -3816 +3816,5 @@
-    elf_bad_symtab (abfd) = true;
+    {
+      elf_bad_symtab (abfd) = true;
+      if (!_bfd_mips_elf_fix_section_alignments (abfd))
+	return false;
+    }
--- a/bfd/elfn32-mips.c
+++ b/bfd/elfn32-mips.c
@@ -3883 +3883,5 @@
-    elf_bad_symtab (abfd) = true;
+    {
+      elf_bad_symtab (abfd) = true;
+      if (!_bfd_mips_elf_fix_section_alignments (abfd))
+	return false;
+    }
--- a/bfd/elfxx-mips.c
+++ b/bfd/elfxx-mips.c
@@ -13123,0 +13124,29 @@
+/* Normalise the section alignments of an SGI input file.
+
+   Upstream commit 1f9b1a84350d3755ce8620900a35c3d1997535e6 (Alan Modra,
+   2022-02-15) made _bfd_elf_make_section_from_shdr read a
+   non-power-of-two sh_addralign as its lowest set bit, so SGI's o32
+   crt1.o, whose .init has sh_addralign 27, becomes alignment 1 and the
+   loader's GOT entry for __istart lands at 2 mod 4, raising an address
+   error.  Older binutils used the largest power of two not exceeding the
+   value (16).  Restore that for SGI inputs only; valid alignments and
+   generic MIPS/Linux objects are untouched.  Modern bfd_log2 rounds up,
+   hence the -1 for a non-power value.  */
+
+bool
+_bfd_mips_elf_fix_section_alignments (bfd *abfd)
+{
+  asection *s;
+
+  for (s = abfd->sections; s != NULL; s = s->next)
+    {
+      bfd_vma align = elf_section_data (s)->this_hdr.sh_addralign;
+
+      if (align > 1 && (align & (align - 1)) != 0)
+	if (!bfd_set_section_alignment (s, bfd_log2 (align) - 1))
+	  return false;
+    }
+
+  return true;
+}
+
--- a/bfd/elfxx-mips.h
+++ b/bfd/elfxx-mips.h
@@ -99,0 +100,2 @@
+extern bool _bfd_mips_elf_fix_section_alignments (bfd *);
+
